{"id": "30004033", "reviewed_at": "2026-09-22T01:03:46+00:00", "statement_hash": "7b9ab2c49e8d662c669d70acbf324c3aabffb2d095668053d4f27235bd695beb", "review_hash": "d397939f95e133e2e7ebf4b1ddc9f815e115371528ac88a3627bfc42a2397681", "review_type": "individual desk triage; not readiness verification", "confidence": "low", "impact": 6, "p_solve": 0.02, "p_valid_open": 0.8, "rationale": "A precise extremal claim with exact finite counterexample certificates and reusable coloring methods. Long history and a recent 11/4 bound make a full proof substantially harder than a small-instance search.", "remaining_gap": "The universal 8/3 bound, not the proved 11/4 or nonplanar 14/5 bounds.", "first_experiment": "Recover the 2025 proof and its excluded configurations; compare exact fractional-coloring LP certificates on small planar subcubic graphs. A finite search only resolves the claim if it finds a verified counterexample.", "holds": [], "sources": ["https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2019/1", "https://www.advancesincombinatorics.com/article/133707-11-4-colorability-of-subcubic-triangle-free-graphs"], "budget": "8 agent-hours exploration + 2 agent-hours independent verification"}
